About Baringa&nbsp;

Baringa is a global consulting firm that partners with leaders to drive change and create value. With deep industry expertise, and enabled by advanced technology, the firm helps clients to deliver with greater confidence and certainty. With over 2,000 people across the UK, Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, the firm combines global insight with local understanding.

The firm works across energy and resources, financial services, government and public sector, consumer products and retail, pharmaceuticals and life sciences, manufacturing, and technology, media and telecoms, with capabilities spanning strategy, transformation and operational excellence - all powered by advanced technology, data, AI and digital innovation.

Clients value Baringa’s collaborative approach and the way its teams integrate seamlessly - all working with a shared understanding of what matters most. The firm is known for its kind, curious experts who listen closely and care deeply about client success as they help clients transform energy markets, modernise financial platforms, expand telecoms and digital networks through advanced data analytics, enable digital services in government, and unlock growth in consumer sectors.

Certified as a&nbsp; Great Place to Work around the world, Baringa has been recognised by the Financial Times in 22 categories of its UK Leading Management Consultants rankings, and by Forbes for four consecutive years as one of the World’s Best Management Consulting Firms.

About the opportunity &nbsp;

We are looking for an experienced Manager to join our growing US consulting team. You will lead teams delivering complex strategic, operational and transformational engagements, working closely with senior clients to define problems, align stakeholders, and turn recommendations into measurable outcomes. You will also play an active role in developing our people, shaping propositions, and growing trusted client relationships. &nbsp;

What you will be doing &nbsp;

• Lead the day-to-day delivery of complex client engagements, with accountability for scope, workplan, quality, risks, team performance and client outcomes. &nbsp;

• Shape approaches to ambiguous business problems and guide teams through analysis, solution design, and implementation planning. &nbsp;

• Build trusted relationships with senior client stakeholders, facilitate decision- making, and communicate clear, evidence-based recommendations. &nbsp;

• Lead multidisciplinary teams, creating clarity and momentum while maintaining high standards of delivery and an inclusive team environment. &nbsp;

• Coach and develop consultants, providing timely feedback, stretch opportunities and support for their career growth. &nbsp;

• Support implementation so that recommendations translate into practical, sustainable change and tangible client benefits. &nbsp;

• Contribute to business development through proposals, account development, market insight, and the creation of reusable capabilities and assets. &nbsp;

• Collaborate across Baringa to bring the right sector, capability and technology expertise to each client challenge. &nbsp;

